  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific standing Gregorian Tower exterior on its retained notched plan: low west chamber/stone balustraded terrace, taller east flat-roofed block/projecting cornice and iron roof rail, small pedimented upper house/pitched cap, sparse recessed closed light shutters, broad pilasters/string courses and bounded buried footings. Existing shared stucco, limestone, painted metal and wood graphs. No fresco/interior, copied coats of arms or inscriptions, photograph atlas, Saint Peter's dome or whole Vatican museum authored.",
    "identityBasis": "Exact-QID retained OSMway176719116 supplies the notched16.997x14.984m tower polygon and undirected axis0.06657450338rad. The current PMTiles has no separate tower building/point at that ID; its footprint lies within palace52776558306308 and touches part35184483819981. Global heading0 and internal axes{\"xAxis\":[0.9977847361323613,-0.06652533608539087],\"zAxis\":[0.06652533608539087,0.9977847361323613]} preserve native east/south placement at12.454195746,41.905161124. West/east stepped mass assignment follows the two pictures and mapped notch; window schedule/directed facade interpretation retain20degree/2m approximation, not surveyed facing.",
    "heightBasis": "Neither retained Wikidata nor tower map geometry supplies a qualified tower height. Picture-led nominal levels: west terrace22.8m, taller east deck30.2m, upper house22.8..27.9m with29.8m pediment/ridge, and roof rails/piers to31.4m above the attachment plane. Neighbor palace17m is a map attribute, not a tower height. Cornice, shutter, terrace, roof-house, ornament and lower hidden wall dimensions are visualization estimates; no73m height datum or modern repair accuracy is asserted.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original6m standard terrain, paths/water and all museum geometry outside the exact tower polygon. Only subtract the overlapping tower area from palace52776558306308 and touching part35184483819981; retain their large remaining footprints and all other independent inputs. A bounded footing sits above the highest occupied rim with buried sides below the lowest. No ground/water cutout, precinct slab or full-palace replacement. Coarse DEM/contact levels and hidden lower walls are visualization estimates; adjoining roof joins must be inspected in native context.",
